From af338a3134d6cca2c6663f9cb27d202b49fdcbaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:22:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-move): unpushed guard scans the move's checkpoint,
 skips other cards' trees, bounds git time, guards the queue repin [daveey]

Follow-ups to PR #1681 (review t_01a1d113d42a1b13; card t_01a1d1197fa00599):
- check()/_card_text scan the move's own checkpoint (it is written after check()).
- a text-named tree whose owner marker names another card is skipped (reviewer naming the implementer's tree).
- tree_state bounds total git time (STATE_BUDGET_S, shrinking per-call timeouts; past it: unchecked = state).
- move_queued's worker-first Board repin to the worker queue takes the unpushed_state_here guard.
- docstring: a move whose matches still include this host is not 'leaving' and is unguarded (intentional).
